{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FaddeevQuantumDilogarithm"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.faddeevPhi_mul_latticeIndicator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.faddeevPhi_mul_latticeIndicator","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FaddeevSolutionSet.lean#L117-L125","doc":"**The witness.** Multiplying any `FaddeevPhi b` solution by the lattice\nindicator gives another `FaddeevPhi b` solution. Since the indicator takes only\nthe values `0` and `1`, the two solutions do NOT have a differentiable ratio\nwherever the indicator is discontinuous — so `hratio` (bean qou-cons) is not\nderivable from the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.latticeIndicator_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.latticeIndicator_zero","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FaddeevSolutionSet.lean#L109-L114","doc":"It is `1` on the lattice — in particular at `0`, so it is not the zero\nfunction, and together with any off-lattice point it is non-constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.latticeIndicator_periodic_binv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.latticeIndicator_periodic_binv","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FaddeevSolutionSet.lean#L97-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.latticeIndicator_periodic_b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.latticeIndicator_periodic_b","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FaddeevSolutionSet.lean#L85-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.latticeIndicator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.latticeIndicator","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FaddeevSolutionSet.lean#L79-L82","doc":"The indicator of the period lattice `ℤ·ib + ℤ·(i/b)`: doubly periodic by\nconstruction, and visibly not continuous anywhere near the lattice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.faddeevPhi_mul_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevSolutionSet.faddeevPhi_mul_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FaddeevSolutionSet.lean#L54-L76","doc":"**The solution set absorbs any doubly-periodic factor**, with no regularity\nasked of it. Both shift equations carry a prefactor that does not see `E`, and\nthe two half-shifts `±ib/2` differ by exactly the period `ib`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}